Subject: [PATCH] hybris/egl/egl.c: hook eglSwapBuffersWithDamageKHR into the swap wrapper

Ported from upstream libhybris PR #565
(https://github.com/libhybris/libhybris/pull/565, commit 5715522,
"hybris: hook eglSwapBuffersWithDamageKHR, add NATIVE_OPERATION_SET_SURFACE_DAMAGE"),
reduced to the minimal interception semantics that our deployed revision needs.

Why the reduction is necessary
------------------------------
PR #565 is written against upstream master, which uses an override table:

    static struct FuncNamePair _eglHybrisOverrideFunctions[] = {
        OVERRIDE_MY(eglSwapBuffersWithDamageEXT),
        OVERRIDE_TO(eglSwapBuffersWithDamageKHR, _my_eglSwapBuffersWithDamageEXT),
        ...
    };

Our deployed revision is Halium/libhybris eaa6884ba95a1d5d0303119ffdc48952a098059b
(libhybris R14, pkgver 1.0_git20191001 pkgrel 14). It has no such table and no
FuncNamePair / OVERRIDE_* machinery at all; its interception is the if/else
chain inside eglGetProcAddress(). So the PR's table change has no counterpart
here and is not imported. The interception is expressed in R14's own idiom.

What is deliberately NOT imported
---------------------------------
1. The PR's new file-scope statics

       static EGLBoolean (*_eglSwapBuffersWithDamageKHR)(...);
       static EGLBoolean (*_eglSwapBuffersWithDamageEXT)(...);

   exist only to let the wrapper *prefer the vendor's damage entry point*.

2. The PR's rewritten swap body, which resolves the vendor damage symbols and
   then calls, in order, vendor KHR -> vendor EXT -> plain vendor eglSwapBuffers.

Neither is required for correctness here, and (2) would change behaviour on the
paths we are required to preserve:

  * The deployed Wayland platform module does not consume the forwarded damage.
    WaylandNativeWindow::finishSwap() issues its own full-surface
    wl_surface_damage(surface, 0, 0, wnb->width, wnb->height) and then clears
    m_damage_rects / m_damage_n_rects, so which vendor damage entry point is
    called does not affect whether a buffer is committed or released.
  * Adopting (2) would also alter the existing eglSwapBuffersWithDamageEXT and
    plain eglSwapBuffers paths, which must be preserved.

The PR's own wayland_window.cpp damage-rect work (NATIVE_WINDOW_SET_SURFACE_DAMAGE,
setSurfaceDamage, the malloc/memcpy of rects, the commented-out FIXME block) is
not imported either: it is damage forwarding, unrelated to the commit path, and
it would require touching the deployed L29 Wayland platform module and
eglplatformcommon, both of which must stay unchanged.

What the existing wrapper already does, unchanged
-------------------------------------------------
Once BOTH names enter it, the R14 wrapper already satisfies the required
semantics verbatim:

    if (egl_helper_has_mapping(surface)) {
        win = egl_helper_get_mapping(surface);
        ws_prepareSwap(dpy, win, rects, n_rects);
        ret = (*_eglSwapBuffers)(dpy, surface);
        ws_finishSwap(dpy, win);
    } else {
        ret = (*_eglSwapBuffers)(dpy, surface);
    }

i.e. mapped window surfaces execute ws_prepareSwap -> vendor swap -> ws_finishSwap,
and unmapped surfaces keep calling the vendor swap alone.

The defect this fixes
---------------------
Gecko resolves one function slot for the damage swap:

    gfx/gl/GLLibraryEGL.cpp:711  fSwapBuffersWithDamage = eglSwapBuffersWithDamageEXT
    gfx/gl/GLLibraryEGL.cpp:724  fSwapBuffersWithDamage = eglSwapBuffersWithDamageKHR
                                 (second branch overwrites the same slot)
    gfx/gl/GLContextProviderEGL.cpp:632  mEgl->fSwapBuffersWithDamage(...)

This device reports both EGL_EXT_swap_buffers_with_damage and
EGL_KHR_swap_buffers_with_damage, so the slot holds the KHR name. With no KHR
arm in eglGetProcAddress, resolution fell through to the vendor, so the client
called PVR's eglSwapBuffersWithDamageKHR directly and never re-entered hybris.
ws_prepareSwap/ws_finishSwap and therefore WaylandNativeWindow::finishSwap() were
never called, no buffer was ever attached or committed, no wl_buffer.release could
ever arrive, m_freeBufs could only decrease, and the 4th dequeueBuffer blocked
forever in readQueue(true) / wl_display_dispatch_queue.

This is the only behavioural change in the patch: one added arm.

Upstream reference
------------------
PR:      https://github.com/libhybris/libhybris/pull/565
Commit:  5715522  "hybris: hook eglSwapBuffersWithDamageKHR, add
                   NATIVE_OPERATION_SET_SURFACE_DAMAGE."
PR claim: "This removes the need for the SailfishOS Gecko workaround
           0047-sailfishos-egl-Drop-swap_buffers_with_damage-extensi.patch",
          which is the same defect: a Gecko-side workaround existed only because
          hybris did not hook the KHR alias. Per instruction, this fix is made on
          the hybris side and Gecko is not patched for this defect.

--- a/egl.c
+++ b/egl.c
@@ -409,6 +409,10 @@ __eglMustCastToProperFunctionPointerType eglGetProcAddress(const char *procn
 	{
 		return (__eglMustCastToProperFunctionPointerType) _my_eglSwapBuffersWithDamageEXT;
 	}
+	else if (strcmp(procname, "eglSwapBuffersWithDamageKHR") == 0)
+	{
+		return (__eglMustCastToProperFunctionPointerType) _my_eglSwapBuffersWithDamageEXT;
+	}
 	else if (strcmp(procname, "glEGLImageTargetTexture2DOES") == 0)
 	{
 		return (__eglMustCastToProperFunctionPointerType) _my_glEGLImageTargetTexture2DOES;
